resources.string:
When the device outputs HDMI at a fixed volume, Android's volume doesn't reach LG NetCast TVs (2013, such as the 42LN5700). The launcher talks to these LG TVs over the home network, after pairing with the code the LG shows on screen.

Once paired, the LG gets the volume from:
• gentle shutdown (the volume goes down gradually);
• the bedtime ceiling;
• volume requests from the phone panel and from Claude;
• the alarm clock, if you turn it on (off by default, and never above 30).

The volume is checked after each change. If the LG's IP changes, the launcher finds the same TV on the network again.

For now, pairing is done from a computer over adb (the lg_pedir_codigo and lg_parear commands). Without a paired LG, everything works with Android's normal volume.
